# EtList

## When to use `EtList` vs `EtTable`

- Use **`EtList`** when each row is one opaque UI element — an `EtAssetItem`, `EtPositionCard`, user card, etc. — and the columns above are just a labeled, optionally sortable header. No horizontal scroll, no fixed column, no per-cell formatting. The body is "a stack of self-rendering rows".
- Use **`EtTable`** (`libs/etoro-ui/src/components/tables/table/`) when rows are composed of cells driven by a column descriptor (`columns: EtTableColumn[]` + `renderColumn(item, column)`), or when you need horizontal column scrolling, a fixed first column, or built-in cell formatters (currency, change%, etc.). The body is "a 2D cell grid".

Concretely:

| | `EtTable.Column` | `EtList.Column` |
|---|---|---|
| What it is | A vertical strip of cells driven by a column descriptor | A single label cell in the header row only |
| Body row composition | `renderColumn(item, column)` per cell | `renderItem({ item })` returns one opaque element |
| Horizontal scroll | Yes | No |
| Fixed-column | Yes | No |

If both could plausibly fit, prefer `EtList` — its API surface is smaller and its mental model ("a list of opaque rows with a labeled header") is closer to what most feature screens actually want.

## Purpose

Generic, virtualized list primitive for the eToro design system. Built with a compound component pattern so consumers compose a list from opinionated subcomponents (`Header`, `Column`, `Skeleton`, `Empty`, `Error`, `Footer`) instead of passing a large structured props blob.

`EtList` is the **only** UI-kit primitive that owns:

- list virtualization (via `@shopify/flash-list`)
- pinned-at-top column headers (rendered as a sibling above the list)
- sortable column cells
- the four-way render-path switch (loading / error / empty / data)

It is intentionally generic — it does not know about asset rows, instrument types, or any feature-level data shape. For asset rows, compose `EtAssetItem` inside `renderItem`. For people rows, build `EtUserItem` (TBD) and compose it inside `renderItem`.

For drag-to-reorder or swipe-to-reveal actions, do **not** add them to `EtList`. Wrap the per-row component (e.g. `EtAssetItem`) with `EtSwipeableRow`, or use a feature-level draggable component (e.g. `draggable-watchlist`).

## Architecture

```text
et-list.tsx (root) → provides ListContext, four render paths driven by `data.length` + `isLoading` + `error`
├── EtList.Header   → pinned-at-top header row; renders `EtList.Column` children
├── EtList.Column   → header cell with optional sortable + sort-direction indicator
├── EtList.Skeleton → initial-loading placeholder rows (renders only when data is empty + isLoading)
├── EtList.Empty    → empty-state slot (renders only when data is empty + not loading + no error)
├── EtList.Error    → initial-load error slot (renders only when data is empty + error is non-null)
└── EtList.Footer   → inline footer rendered as the FlashList's ListFooterComponent (scrolls into view)
```

